          lemma: "Ἐγώ εἰμι",
          title: "“I am he”",
          body: "The Greek is simply **ἐγώ εἰμι**, *“I am”* — and to a woman, a Samaritan, an outsider, Jesus grants what he mostly hides from the crowds: an open claim to be the Messiah. The phrase also rings with the divine name of Exodus 3:14 and Isaiah (“I am he,” Isa 43:10), a note John will strike again and again (8:58). The first person in this Gospel to hear it plainly is the least likely — and she becomes its first missionary.",
