          lemma: "ἀφῆκεν τὴν ὑδρίαν",
          title: "She left her water-jar",
          body: "A small, telling detail: she **leaves the very jar** she came for. The thing that brought her to the well no longer matters; she has found the living water and runs to tell others — the errand forgotten, like nets left on a shore. John, who noticed the disciples leaving their labor (1:14; and cf. the jars of ch. 2), lets an abandoned pot preach.",
