          id: 'a4.29.1',
          kind: "grammar",
          refs: ['g4.29.10', 'g4.29.14'],
          lemma: "μήτι οὗτός ἐστιν",
          title: "“Could this be…?” — a hopeful maybe",
          body: "The little particle **μήτι** frames a question that *expects the answer “no”* — so her words are tentative, almost shy: “This couldn’t be the Christ… could it?” It is exactly the right note for a witness: she does not lecture, she invites — **“Come, see”** (the same words Jesus and Philip used, 1:39, 46) — and lets the town meet him for themselves. Understated testimony is often the most disarming.",
