      annotations: [
        {
          id: 'a4.34.1',
          kind: "concept",
          refs: ['g4.34.6', 'g4.34.16'],
          lemma: "Ἐμὸν βρῶμα … τελειώσω",
          title: "“My food is to do the will of him who sent me”",
          body: "The disciples worry about lunch; Jesus has just been fed. His true nourishment is the Father’s **will** and the completing of his **work** — the verb **τελειόω**, *to bring to completion*, points ahead to the cross, where he will say **“It is finished”** (19:30). Doing the Father’s will is not a duty draining him but the very thing that sustains him. And its first course has just been served: one Samaritan woman, and a town on its way out to meet him.",
        },
      ],
