          refs: ['g4.48.9', 'g4.48.11', 'g4.48.15'],
          lemma: "σημεῖα καὶ τέρατα",
          title: "“Signs and wonders”",
          body: "The rebuke is aimed wider than one man — the “you” is plural (**ἴδητε**, **πιστεύσητε**). John draws a persistent line between faith that *demands* a spectacle and faith that simply *takes Jesus at his word*. The official is being invited across that line: he came wanting Jesus to come *down* and *do* something visible; he will leave having believed a bare sentence (v. 50). Signs are given — but they are meant to lead to trusting the person, not to replace it.",
