          body: "John explicitly numbers this the **second sign** Jesus did on coming from Judea to Galilee, tying it back to the **first** at the same Cana (2:11). The two frame the section like bookends — water-to-wine and word-to-life — and both end in *believing*. It is a reminder that John has selected and shaped his “signs” (there are seven) as a deliberate sequence, written “so that you may believe” (20:30–31).",
